    "The ablation C row is the fully converged resumed run (best epoch 49, 50 epochs total), not the earlier under-trained checkpoint.",
    "Robustness numbers use one fixed 30,000-record test subset (12,520 known U/D) and do not include confidence intervals; no error bars are drawn.",
    "Ablation A/B stopped before the 50-epoch schedule completed and their run metadata does not record completed epochs; C was resumed to 50 epochs and D reuses the final SOPNet checkpoint. A/B absolute scores should therefore be read as not fully converged, and A/B-vs-C/D gaps cannot be attributed solely to the loss terms."
